{"Title":"An Act relative to monthly minimum reliability contributions","BillNumber":"S2130","DocketNumber":"SD71","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"AMG0","Name":"Anne M. Gobi","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AMG0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T13:48:27.013"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"AMG0","Name":"Anne M. Gobi","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AMG0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T13:48:27.0133333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2130/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Gobi, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2130) of Anne M. Gobi for legislation relative to monthly minimum reliability contributions.  Telecommunications, Utilities and Energy.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 139 of Chapter 164 of the General Laws, as amended by Section 9 of Chapter 75 of the Acts of 2016, is hereby amended by striking the first sentence of the third paragraph of subsection (j) and inserting in place thereof the following:-\r\n\tThe department shall exempt from any monthly minimum reliability contribution the following: municipal ratepayers, low-income ratepayers, community solar ratepayers, and owners of small-scale solar projects of 25 kilowatts or less.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J37","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J37"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}